    "result": "The frai-core suite now passes: 8 files, 28 tests. I didn't touch any test files, and every existing export still works.\n\nThere were two bugs:\n\n- **Toxicity score (`src/eval/metrics.js`):** The default metrics run as `(outputs, references)`. `toxicityMetric` treated its second argument as the banned-terms list, so the references (\"hello\", \"friendly world\") became banned terms and flagged the outputs. The default entry in `DEFAULT_METRICS` is now a wrapper, `(outputs) => toxicityMetric(outputs)`, which uses the built-in banned terms. `toxicityMetric` itself is unchanged.\n- **`APPROVAL_STATUSES` (`src/finetune/index.js`):** The module imported the constant and put it on the default export, but never exported it by name. The governance test imports it by name, so it got `undefined`. I added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS` and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
